  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1142 PM MST Sun Nov 8 2026\n\nUpper level ridging over the Great Basin and troughing over the \nGreat Plains Wednesday helps sends a backdoor front through eastern \nNM during the morning hours resulting in some breezy north winds \nthrough early Wednesday afternoon. The GFS has now come in line with \nthe other mid range guidance keeping max wind gusts in the 20 to 30 \nmph range. The upper ridge slides east over the state Wednesday \nnight into Thursday before sliding east of the state late Friday. \nThis will allow the tranquil November weather to continue! High to \nmid level clouds move in from the west Friday evening into Saturday \nmorning as an upper low moves into northern Baja CA. Deterministic \nand ensemble guidance has now trended further south with the track \nof the weakening upper low taking it across northern Mexico Saturday \ninto Saturday night. This will keep most shower activity across \nsouthern NM. Skies somewhat clear during the day Sunday in the wake \nof this system and ahead of a larger scale upper level trough over \nthe Pacific NW and Great Basin. High temperatures mid to late this \nweek will be near to as much as 10 degrees above average for mid \nNovember. Slight cooling across eastern NM Wednesday compared to \nTuesday due to the backdoor front. Low temperatures will be 5 to 12 \ndegrees above average for mid November.",
